  "description": "PR #482 dropped pipeline snapshots for URLs that we knew the \
pipeline could not currently regenerate. Put those snapshots back once the \
remaining Paprika-export coverage gaps are closed.\n\
\n\
This issue is blocked on the union of the outstanding split issues created out \
of the old umbrella tracker:\n\
\n\
  - `p3-add-html-fallback-extraction-for-cocktailswithsuderman-substack`\n\
  - `p3-add-html-fallback-extraction-for-virtualweberbullet-recipes`\n\
  - `p3-add-html-fallback-extraction-for-pre-schema-smitten-kitchen-posts`\n\
  - `p3-add-html-fallback-extraction-for-seriouseats-pages-with-bad-schema`\n\
  - `p3-add-localhost-bookmarklet-capture-for-bot-walled-pipeline-urls`\n\
\n\
Bucket C is intentionally not listed as a blocker here because the current \
belief is that we already handled it. If that turns out to be wrong, add the \
missing bucket C follow-up as another blocker before doing the snapshot \
restore.\n\
\n\
When this unblocks, the implementation work should rerun `make pipeline`, \
restore the dropped snapshot files, and commit the resulting `data/` diffs so \
reviewers can see exactly what coverage came back.",
